  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**:\n\n\ud83d\udd17 **https://www.python.org/downloads/**\n\nThe latest version is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions.\n\nPython 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\nHere are some highlights about what's new in Python 3.14:\n\n- **Free-threaded Python** is now officially supported (PEP 779), and the evaluation of annotations is now deferred, improving the semantics of using annotations (PEP 649).\n- **Template string literals (t-strings)** for custom string processing, using the familiar syntax of f-strings (PEP 750).\n- A new module **compression.zstd** providing support for the Zstandard compression algorithm (PEP 784).\n\n### Platform-specific downloads:\n- **Windows**: The installer for Windows is being replaced by a new install manager, which can be installed from the Windows Store or from its download page.\n- **macOS & Linux**: Installers and source code are available directly on the [downloads page](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\n- **Source code**: Available at https://www.python.org/downloads/source/\n\nAlways make sure to download Python from the **official python.org website** to ensure you're getting a safe and verified version.",
